<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Transcaucasian SFSR</h1><p class="st-meta">1922 CE – 1936 CE · capital Tiflis</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Soviet federation of Georgia, Armenia and Azerbaijan from 1922 to 1936, a founding member of the USSR.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1922 the Soviet republics of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgia">Georgia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> were joined in a union, which in December 1922 became the Transcaucasian Socialist Federative Soviet Republic with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tiflis</a>. On 30 December 1922 it was one of the four founding republics of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The federation was driven by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow's</a> wish to control the region's economy, railways and borders and to damp national rivalries. Georgian communists who opposed it lost out to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-stalin">Stalin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sergo-ordzhonikidze">Ordzhonikidze</a> in the so-called Georgian Affair. It shared a single government, while the three republics kept their own institutions. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavrentiy-beria">Lavrentiy Beria</a> led its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Communist Party</a> from 1932.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the 1936 Soviet constitution the federation was dissolved, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/georgian-ssr">Georgian SSR</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenian-ssr">Armenian SSR</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan-ssr">Azerbaijan SSR</a> became separate union republics of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>. Each of the three later became independent within its Soviet borders in 1991.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/transcaucasian-sfsr.jpg" alt="Transcaucasian SFSR" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: en:User:Aivazovsky · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Transcaucasian_SFSR_(variant).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1922 CE – 1936 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tiflis</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sergo Ordzhonikidze, Lavrentiy Beria</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian; Georgian; Armenian; Azerbaijani</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Georgia, Armenia, Azerbaijan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Transcaucasian Socialist Federative Soviet Republic, ZSFSR</dd></dl></aside></div>
